Date: Fri, 6 Nov 2026 12:30:35 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 617/619] dt-bindings: phy: mediatek,tphy: add the U2 squelch
 threshold

The T-PHY driver writes a fixed squelch threshold of 2 to every U2 port.
The MT6797's USB11 port receives with the hardware default of 8, which
the vendor kernel never changes. Add an optional per-port
mediatek,rx-sqth to name the value.
---
 Documentation/devicetree/bindings/phy/mediatek,tphy.yaml | 9 +++++++++
 1 file changed, 9 insertions(+)

diff --git a/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/phy/mediatek,tphy.yaml b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/phy/mediatek,tphy.yaml
index 16afd2f0a..eb213fda2 100644
--- a/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/phy/mediatek,tphy.yaml
+++ b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/phy/mediatek,tphy.yaml
@@ -248,6 +248,15 @@ patternProperties:
           Specify the flag to enable BC1.2 if support it
         type: boolean
 
+      mediatek,rx-sqth:
+        description:
+          The U2 receiver's squelch threshold. Without it the driver sets 2;
+          a port whose receiver needs another value, often the hardware
+          default, names it here.
+        $ref: /schemas/types.yaml#/definitions/uint32
+        minimum: 0
+        maximum: 15
+
       mediatek,force-b-session-valid:
         description:
           Force the USB2 PHY session signals to a valid B-device state. This
